# Read-only replay row data can contain customer identifiers and exceed GitHub's
# file limit. Keep the reproducible scripts and sanitized Markdown summaries.
/docs/creative-decision-center/generated/exact-pit-confirmatory-replay-*.json
/docs/creative-decision-center/generated/native-ad-grain-paired-replay-*.json
/docs/creative-decision-center/generated/native-structure-grain-paired-replay-*.json
/docs/creative-decision-center/generated/h1-country-parent-challenger-*.json
/docs/creative-decision-center/generated/h11-campaign-context-challenger-*.json
/docs/creative-decision-center/generated/h12-decision-hysteresis-challenger-*.json
# PRE-DEPLOY AUDIT 2026-09-03, CORRECTED 2026-09-03: the same class as above —
# with one entry removed, because the claim that justified it was false.
#
# The removed pattern was
# `/docs/creative-decision-center/generated/h11b-context-lifecycle-bundle-*.json`,
# excused as "generator OUTPUT that no test reads from disk". It is read from
# disk, by exact path AND by pinned SHA-256, at
# `scripts/audits/d082-meta-role-provenance-replay.ts:99`
# (`D082_PINNED_INPUTS.h11bBundlePath`). Ignoring it made D082 pass only
# because the file happened to be sitting in this working tree: a clean
# checkout has no such file, and D082 would refuse on a missing pinned input.
# It is therefore tracked, and
# `scripts/audits/d082-clean-checkout-inventory.test.ts` now proves every D082
# pinned input survives a clean-checkout-equivalent inventory, so no future
# ignore rule can silently take one away again.
#
# The two below were re-checked the same way and are genuinely unread:
# the h11 regression path is the challenger's own `JSON_OUT`
# (`h11-campaign-context-challenger.ts:58`) and nothing reads it back, and the
# account-scoped shadow file has no reader anywhere in app/, components/, lib/
# or scripts/.
/docs/creative-decision-center/generated/h11-campaign-context-v2-posthoc-regression-*.json
/docs/creative-decision-center/generated/automatic-campaign-context-shadow-account-scoped-*.json

# Local prompt/correction files written beside the repo by the coding agents.
# They are working notes, never part of a release.
.codex-tmp-*

# PRE-DEPLOY AUDIT 2026-09-03 — generated audit evidence that NO test opens.
#
# Almost all of docs/audits/generated/ is deliberately COMMITTED: those
# artifacts are hash-pinned and read from disk by the D077-D086 acceptance
# tests, so excluding them turns the suite red. The set was resolved by
# following the test import closure, not by grepping basenames — several are
# reached through an exported constant (`PIT_REPLAY_JSON_OUT`, `D084_JSON_OUT`)
# or through a pinned-predecessor table the test iterates and `readFileSync`s
# (`D084_SUPERSEDES.priorChain`), so a basename grep says "unused" about files
# the suite hard-requires.
#
# These two are what is left: a shell transcript and a screenshot directory,
# both run output that no test opens and that re-running regenerates.
/docs/audits/generated/*.log
# PRE-DEPLOY AUDIT 2026-09-03, CORRECTED: except the canonical whole-shell
# captures. `lib/meta/__tests__/d077-artifact-hash-contract.test.ts` opens the
# retained log by the path the ledger pins and refuses when it is missing
# ("the portable whole-shell log is MISSING at … — fail-closed"), and the
# release-candidate manifest pins it too. The blanket rule above excluded BOTH
# the 2026-08-30 and the 2026-09-03 capture, so D077 could not have been
# reproduced from a clean checkout — the same defect class as the H11b bundle,
# found the same way: a claim that "no test opens it" that nobody checked
# against the readers.
!/docs/audits/generated/d077-canonical-database-seams-whole-shell-*.log
/docs/audits/generated/d078-local-ui-screenshots/

# Playwright evidence: the AUTHENTICATED receipts are read at module scope by
# scripts/audits/d084-evidence-receipts.test.ts and therefore stay tracked. The
# static-harness directory beside it is `existsSync`-guarded and is run output.
playwright/.evidence/d084-budget-evidence/

# Transient Playwright smoke output. Kept evidence lives in dated subdirectories
# (e.g. playwright-smoke-artifacts/<name>-<date>/), which stay tracked; these two
# paths are rewritten by every run and must not accumulate in the tree.
/docs/full-ui-redesign/playwright-smoke-artifacts/html-report/
/docs/full-ui-redesign/playwright-smoke-artifacts/test-results/
playwright/.harness/
playwright/.frames/
playwright/.runtime/
